        "attempt": 1,
        "status": "OK",
        "duration_seconds": 57.291,
        "asr_text": "At restaurants, cafes, and in taxis, payment screens may ask how much you would like to tip. One large study looked specifically at New York City taxis, where a screen shows several suggested tip rates before payment. In 2014, researchers published this peer-reviewed study in the American Economic Journal: Applied Economics. They studied more than 13 million credit card payments in New York City taxis. Before payment, the screen showed a small menu of suggested tip rates. When the fare was just below or just above $15, the menu changed. Suddenly, this gave the researchers a useful comparison. They used a method called regression discontinuity. In simple terms, they compared rides that were almost the same but showed different tip menus.",
