        "status": "OK",
        "duration_seconds": 36.331,
        "asr_text": "The result was clear: passengers who happened to see higher suggested rates left more money. In this study, the first number on the screen became a starting point for their decision. But a high suggestion does not always bring a higher tip. When the suggested rate feels too high, some customers do not choose a smaller custom amount. Instead, they leave no tip on the credit card. So the screen has two possible effects: it can guide some people toward a larger tip, but it can also make other people choose zero.",
